<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kumtor Gold Mine</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kumtor Gold Mine is an open-pit gold mine high in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tian-shan">Tian Shan</a> mountains of Kyrgyzstan, south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/issyk-kul">Lake Issyk-Kul</a>, at about 4,000 metres. Developed with a Canadian company and producing from 1997, it became the country's largest industrial enterprise and a large share of its exports and output. The Kyrgyz government took control of the mine in 2021 and full ownership in 2022.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kumtor-gold-mine.jpg" alt="Kumtor Gold Mine" width="320" height="141" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Michael Karavanov · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kumtor_Gold_Mine_-_panoramio_-_Michael_Karavanov.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
